# G
## I
This is exactly the right mindset. Moving from a sprawling static repository to a structured, dynamic backend is the only way you’re going to support API calls, AI integrations, and gated token sessions cleanly. 

Since you are planning for async AI calls (like fetching literature reviews) and high-performance workflows in the future, **FastAPI** is the superior choice over Flask. It natively supports asynchronous operations (crucial for waiting on AI responses without blocking other users) and generates automatic API documentation.

Here is your automated "zero manual work" solution. This `setup.sh` script will prompt you for your credentials, generate the exact minimal FastAPI scaffolding (focusing only on Levels 1-3 and Sessions 1-5), set up a basic token-gating structure, create the repository on GitHub, and prep it for automated Render deployment.

### **The Automation Script (`setup.sh`)**

Create a new file named `setup.sh` on your machine, paste the following code into it, and run it. 

```bash
#!/bin/bash

# ==========================================
# 1. GATHER CREDENTIALS & INFO
# ==========================================
clear
echo "🚀 Welcome to the Dynamic Backend Setup 🚀"
echo "We are building a FastAPI app ready for Render and AI integration."
echo "--------------------------------------------------------------"

read -p "Enter your GitHub Username: " GITHUB_USER
read -p "Enter your GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT): " GITHUB_TOKEN
read -p "Enter the new GitHub Repository Name (e.g., dynamic-classes): " REPO_NAME
read -p "Is this repo private or public? (private/public): " REPO_PRIVACY
read -p "Set a default access token (password) for your classes: " CLASS_TOKEN

if [ "$REPO_PRIVACY" == "private" ]; then
    PRIVACY_FLAG="true"
else
    PRIVACY_FLAG="false"
fi

# ==========================================
# 2. SCAFFOLD DIRECTORY STRUCTURE
# ==========================================
echo -e "\n📁 Scaffolding directories..."
mkdir -p $REPO_NAME/app/templates/partials
mkdir -p $REPO_NAME/app/static/css
mkdir -p $REPO_NAME/app/static/js
cd $REPO_NAME

# Create Level and Session templates
for level in {1..3}; do
    for session in {1..5}; do
        mkdir -p app/templates/level${level}/session${session}
        echo "<h1>Level $level - Session $session</h1><p>Content goes here.</p>" > app/templates/level${level}/session${session}/index.html
    done
done

# ==========================================
# 3. GENERATE CORE FILES
# ==========================================
echo "🐍 Generating FastAPI Backend..."

# requirements.txt
cat <<EOF > requirements.txt
fastapi
uvicorn
jinja2
python-multipart
EOF

# .gitignore
cat <<EOF > .gitignore
... [TRUNCATED]

